WEBVTT

00:00:02.480 --> 00:00:04.980
It's almost time for the school festival.

00:00:04.980 --> 00:00:08.070
I've loved festivals ever since we went to the summer festival.

00:00:09.320 --> 00:00:11.620
You must be very excited.

00:00:11.620 --> 00:00:13.030
By the way, Alice...

00:00:13.030 --> 00:00:17.070
I can't help but feel that you may have the wrong idea.

00:00:17.370 --> 00:00:20.290
A school festival isn't like those kinds of festivals.

00:00:20.290 --> 00:00:21.040
What?

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:24.750
Our class is going to run a café.

00:00:25.290 --> 00:00:29.830
We're currently split over whether we
should do a maid café or a Japanese café.

00:00:29.830 --> 00:00:31.400
Which do you two like more?

00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:32.670
A maid café!
A Japanese café!

00:00:36.840 --> 00:00:39.560
I don't wish to fight, but you leave me no choice.

00:00:40.060 --> 00:00:42.350
I won't go easy on you, Alice.

00:00:43.140 --> 00:00:44.350
What are you even fighting for?

00:00:44.770 --> 00:00:46.610
If you don't stand down...

00:00:47.690 --> 00:00:49.980
...I won't go with you to the bathroom at night!

00:00:53.530 --> 00:00:56.450
That has nothing to do with this!

00:00:56.820 --> 00:01:00.410
If you don't pick the Japanese café instead, I will hate you!

00:01:00.410 --> 00:01:02.010
What?

00:01:02.010 --> 00:01:03.700
B-But I...

00:01:09.210 --> 00:01:11.800
J-Japanese...

00:01:11.800 --> 00:01:13.260
Maid...

00:01:13.630 --> 00:01:16.610
Is this really such a serious issue?

00:01:16.610 --> 00:01:18.510
Why not combine the two, then?

00:01:18.510 --> 00:01:20.760
It'll be a true cultural exchange!

00:01:23.770 --> 00:01:25.230
That's a good idea.

00:01:25.230 --> 00:01:28.020
Both of us can agree to that.

00:01:29.770 --> 00:01:31.940
How about we do this?

00:01:31.940 --> 00:01:34.530
Heave-ho, heave-ho, heave-ho!

00:01:34.900 --> 00:01:39.100
We'll carry Shino, dressed as a maid, on a palanquin.

00:01:39.100 --> 00:01:41.020
It fits Alice's image of a festival, too.

00:01:41.020 --> 00:01:42.030
That's not a bad idea.

00:01:42.490 --> 00:01:46.540
<i>I don't want a café like that...</i>

00:01:47.210 --> 00:01:49.040
I'm glad we got everything ready in time.

00:01:49.040 --> 00:01:50.040
Me, too.

00:01:50.590 --> 00:01:53.000
My class is putting on a play.

00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:55.010
I hope you'll all come see it.

00:01:55.380 --> 00:01:57.720
I'll visit your café, too.

00:01:57.720 --> 00:01:59.390
Are you going to be in the play?

00:01:59.390 --> 00:02:01.220
I am!

00:02:01.220 --> 00:02:02.390
Amazing.

00:02:02.760 --> 00:02:07.510
My role is a <i>se-cret</i>...

00:02:07.510 --> 00:02:10.810
But you can expect big things from me.

00:02:10.810 --> 00:02:13.020
I'll save you some good seats.

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:16.990
She has the aura of a real actress...

00:03:48.360 --> 00:03:51.870
Comedy is important to educators in this day and age.

00:03:52.110 --> 00:03:54.940
Students like funny teachers.

00:03:59.700 --> 00:04:03.040
<i>They need to make jokes... jokes...</i>

00:04:03.040 --> 00:04:05.390
<i>Jokes... Jokes...</i>

00:04:08.180 --> 00:04:10.060
A totem pole!

00:04:14.730 --> 00:04:17.270
Uh, u-um, Sensei...

00:04:17.270 --> 00:04:18.480
Yes?

00:04:19.780 --> 00:04:21.780
This is our class's festival application form.

00:04:22.150 --> 00:04:24.910
We're sharing the responsibility of the costumes.

00:04:24.910 --> 00:04:27.640
This looks fun.

00:04:27.640 --> 00:04:30.540
By the way, Komichi-san...

00:04:30.870 --> 00:04:31.540
Yes?

00:04:31.910 --> 00:04:34.370
Feel free to comment on my joke.

00:04:34.370 --> 00:04:35.210
What?

00:04:35.880 --> 00:04:37.460
<i>That was a joke?</i>

00:04:37.750 --> 00:04:38.880
Come on.

00:04:38.880 --> 00:04:40.960
I couldn't possibly comment, Sensei.

00:04:40.960 --> 00:04:42.840
Don't be shy!

00:04:44.230 --> 00:04:45.680
I-I know.

00:04:45.680 --> 00:04:47.890
If you're looking for a response, I know just the person.

00:04:50.510 --> 00:04:52.020
Youko!

00:04:52.020 --> 00:04:53.770
Inokuma-san!

00:04:54.850 --> 00:04:56.270
What? What?

00:05:05.700 --> 00:05:07.950
This is called Kintaro Candy.

00:05:07.950 --> 00:05:11.050
No matter how much you cut it, Kintaro still stares out at you.

00:05:12.620 --> 00:05:14.210
Is it that unusual?

00:05:14.210 --> 00:05:16.290
There are so many Shino faces!

00:05:17.630 --> 00:05:21.340
Everything in Japan looks just like you, Shino.

00:05:21.340 --> 00:05:22.800
Kintaro...

00:05:37.100 --> 00:05:39.020
Maybe we should shorten it a little.

00:05:39.020 --> 00:05:40.420
Alice.

00:05:41.770 --> 00:05:42.900
You can go now.

00:05:42.900 --> 00:05:44.030
Thanks.

00:05:45.360 --> 00:05:46.360
What?

00:05:46.360 --> 00:05:49.530
We're in charge of making the menus.

00:05:49.530 --> 00:05:50.740
Yeah.

00:05:50.740 --> 00:05:53.540
We came up with the menu together, after all.

00:05:53.880 --> 00:05:56.290
Where's the nearest store?

00:05:56.290 --> 00:05:58.610
Probably the hardware store in Kitaguchi.

00:05:58.610 --> 00:06:01.290
Hey, Aya. Let's go!

00:06:01.840 --> 00:06:02.670
Wait up.

00:06:02.670 --> 00:06:04.800
Aya, where are you going?

00:06:04.800 --> 00:06:07.300
To buy materials.

00:06:09.970 --> 00:06:12.010
Will you go grab the tea?

00:06:12.010 --> 00:06:13.450
Sure.

00:06:15.560 --> 00:06:19.690
Baking chocolate, canned red beans, rice flour...

00:06:19.690 --> 00:06:21.610
I want hamburgers today.

00:06:21.610 --> 00:06:22.820
Now, listen...

00:06:23.230 --> 00:06:25.590
What do you want tonight?

00:06:25.590 --> 00:06:26.900
Hamburgers, maybe?

00:06:29.070 --> 00:06:31.910
We're just friends, you hear?!

00:06:31.910 --> 00:06:33.280
Where did that come from?

00:06:37.750 --> 00:06:38.290
Huh?

00:06:38.590 --> 00:06:39.870
Karasu-chan?

00:06:39.870 --> 00:06:40.930
Ah.

00:06:40.930 --> 00:06:42.290
You found me.

00:06:42.710 --> 00:06:44.550
Are you buying supplies for the festival?

00:06:44.550 --> 00:06:45.820
Yes.

00:06:45.820 --> 00:06:47.380
How about you?

00:06:47.380 --> 00:06:49.170
I'm just picking up some snacks.

00:06:50.090 --> 00:06:52.300
If you eat at this hour, you'll get fat.

00:06:52.300 --> 00:06:53.550
Don't worry.

00:06:53.830 --> 00:06:55.560
It's tofu.

00:06:56.140 --> 00:06:58.060
<i>Tofu... as a snack?</i>

00:06:58.060 --> 00:07:00.190
<i>She's even buying soy sauce.</i>

00:07:01.810 --> 00:07:02.810
We're back.

00:07:02.810 --> 00:07:04.320
Welcome back.

00:07:04.320 --> 00:07:06.070
You're all working hard.

00:07:07.280 --> 00:07:09.070
Komichi-san.

00:07:09.490 --> 00:07:13.160
Can you try on your outfit to see if it fits?

00:07:13.160 --> 00:07:13.840
What?

00:07:13.840 --> 00:07:16.040
I thought I was wearing a Japanese outfit.

00:07:16.040 --> 00:07:16.560
Huh?

00:07:16.560 --> 00:07:17.450
But...

00:07:17.450 --> 00:07:19.500
Inokuma-san and Oomiya-san said...

00:07:19.870 --> 00:07:22.420
No matter how you look at it, you've got to wear this.

00:07:22.420 --> 00:07:24.040
I think it'll look great on you.

00:07:24.040 --> 00:07:25.880
Don't just decide that!

00:07:55.660 --> 00:07:58.580
Preparing everything was a lot of work, but I'm really excited.

00:07:58.580 --> 00:07:59.290
Yeah.

00:07:59.620 --> 00:08:01.330
By the way, Shino...

00:08:01.330 --> 00:08:03.540
Do you remember what day tomorrow is?

00:08:03.540 --> 00:08:05.000
The day of the school festival, right?

00:08:05.000 --> 00:08:07.380
No, besides that.

00:08:07.380 --> 00:08:08.450
Besides that?

00:08:08.450 --> 00:08:09.800
Um...

00:08:10.230 --> 00:08:16.380
<i>It's not a holiday, and it's not anyone's birthday.</i>

00:08:21.560 --> 00:08:22.890
<i>An anniversary?</i>

00:08:23.690 --> 00:08:24.560
Of what?

00:08:27.310 --> 00:08:28.980
You don't remember?

00:08:28.980 --> 00:08:30.570
Oh, no.

00:08:30.990 --> 00:08:32.700
I remember!

00:08:32.700 --> 00:08:35.510
It's a very important day for you, right?

00:08:36.240 --> 00:08:38.900
Um, what is it?

00:08:38.900 --> 00:08:41.330
It's, uh... I know!

00:08:41.330 --> 00:08:43.370
It's the day you spoke your first word!

00:08:43.370 --> 00:08:44.670
No.

00:08:44.670 --> 00:08:46.420
The day you first went to the beach.

00:08:46.420 --> 00:08:47.580
No.

00:08:47.920 --> 00:08:51.590
T-The day you took your first steps...

00:08:51.590 --> 00:08:54.550
Uh, um...

00:08:54.550 --> 00:08:56.390
Forget it!

00:09:01.810 --> 00:09:06.130
<i>Alice is sad because I can't remember what tomorrow is.</i>

00:09:12.480 --> 00:09:14.820
<i>I have to remember soon.</i>

00:09:14.820 --> 00:09:16.660
<i>Before I go to sleep...</i>

00:09:25.660 --> 00:09:27.860
Listen, Shino.

00:09:27.860 --> 00:09:29.220
Tomorrow's the day-

00:09:41.850 --> 00:09:43.850
Good morning.

00:09:45.850 --> 00:09:47.350
What's wrong, Alice?

00:09:47.350 --> 00:09:48.740
You look like an octopus.

00:09:49.610 --> 00:09:50.610
Octy!

00:09:50.610 --> 00:09:52.430
Don't be rude.

00:09:52.430 --> 00:09:54.070
She's mad.

00:09:54.070 --> 00:09:55.670
Oh, right.

00:09:55.670 --> 00:09:56.700
I'm sorry...

00:09:57.110 --> 00:09:57.910
You look like a squid.

00:09:57.910 --> 00:09:59.570
That's no different!

00:10:00.320 --> 00:10:05.580
Alice has been upset since yesterday because I can't remember what anniversary it is today.

00:10:05.580 --> 00:10:06.800
Anniversary?

00:10:06.800 --> 00:10:07.980
Alice!

00:10:08.670 --> 00:10:09.960
I give up.

00:10:11.500 --> 00:10:12.710
I'm sorry.

00:10:13.050 --> 00:10:14.960
It's because I'm so stupid.

00:10:16.300 --> 00:10:17.130
It's okay.

00:10:17.130 --> 00:10:18.800
I should be apologising to you.

00:10:18.800 --> 00:10:20.000
I've got it!

00:10:20.000 --> 00:10:21.800
Hit me!

00:10:21.800 --> 00:10:23.760
The shock may help me remember!

00:10:23.760 --> 00:10:24.520
What?

00:10:24.520 --> 00:10:26.010
Come on! Do it now!

00:10:26.010 --> 00:10:26.980
Whack me hard!

00:10:26.980 --> 00:10:29.770
S-Shino, it's okay.

00:10:33.320 --> 00:10:37.360
Today's the day you came to stay with me in England.

00:10:37.360 --> 00:10:39.400
That's the anniversary?

00:10:39.400 --> 00:10:40.110
Yup.

00:10:40.690 --> 00:10:43.080
We throw a party every year.

00:10:48.790 --> 00:10:50.920
<i>And then Shinobu...</i>

00:10:52.040 --> 00:10:56.840
We prepare a feast and reminisce about you over dinner.

00:10:56.840 --> 00:10:59.420
We call it the Shino anniversary.

00:10:59.710 --> 00:11:01.510
You're embarrassing me.

00:11:01.510 --> 00:11:02.800
<i>Every year?</i>

00:11:02.800 --> 00:11:05.360
<i>There can't be </i>that<i> much to talk about.</i>

00:11:05.360 --> 00:11:07.810
I had no idea it was my anniversary.

00:11:08.230 --> 00:11:10.520
It's embarrassing, but it also makes me happy.

00:11:10.520 --> 00:11:12.690
So, anyway...

00:11:12.690 --> 00:11:14.610
I want an anniversary, too!

00:11:14.610 --> 00:11:17.110
Why don't you make your acting debut an anniversary?

00:11:17.110 --> 00:11:19.780
You can call it "Karen's Debut" anniversary.

00:11:19.780 --> 00:11:21.540
Great idea.

00:11:21.540 --> 00:11:23.200
You're not an actress.

00:11:23.200 --> 00:11:26.080
What about an Academy Award anniversary?

00:11:26.080 --> 00:11:28.200
That's even more far-fetched!

00:11:31.370 --> 00:11:34.960
<i>I guess it's fine as long as I give it to her sometime today.</i>

00:11:47.970 --> 00:11:50.230
I'm a Victorian maid.

00:11:56.460 --> 00:11:58.690
Aya-chan, you look great.

00:11:58.690 --> 00:12:00.190
You're so cute.

00:12:00.190 --> 00:12:01.400
So cute.

00:12:01.770 --> 00:12:04.280
Stop!

00:12:04.950 --> 00:12:06.780
Japanese tea in teacups.

00:12:07.200 --> 00:12:09.040
Coffee in Japanese cups.

00:12:09.490 --> 00:12:11.040
Red bean cake.

00:12:11.410 --> 00:12:13.420
Chocolate dangos.

00:12:13.420 --> 00:12:16.740
This café is just like us.

00:12:16.740 --> 00:12:18.050
You're right.

00:12:19.880 --> 00:12:21.850
It's a café of chaos.

00:12:22.670 --> 00:12:23.710
Get ready, girls!

00:12:23.710 --> 00:12:26.220
We've got customers coming in.

00:12:26.590 --> 00:12:28.720
Okay.

00:12:30.350 --> 00:12:32.230
Welcome.

00:12:33.600 --> 00:12:34.490
Huh?

00:12:34.490 --> 00:12:36.560
Adults are coming in.

00:12:36.560 --> 00:12:38.520
They're members of the public.

00:12:39.440 --> 00:12:40.820
Welcome.

00:12:40.820 --> 00:12:42.650
Please sit wherever you like.

00:12:42.650 --> 00:12:45.180
W-Welcome.

00:12:45.180 --> 00:12:47.400
Japanese is so hard.

00:12:48.280 --> 00:12:51.940
You're a maid, so you'll have to call people "Master".

00:12:53.460 --> 00:12:54.150
Come on.

00:12:54.150 --> 00:12:55.360
You've got customers.

00:12:56.110 --> 00:12:57.790
Guess I have to...

00:12:57.790 --> 00:13:01.860
W-Welcome, M-M-M-

00:13:03.510 --> 00:13:05.170
What kind of sound effect is that?

00:13:05.930 --> 00:13:08.180
Karasuma-sensei, welcome.

00:13:08.640 --> 00:13:11.430
Please try these dangos we made with love!

00:13:11.430 --> 00:13:12.950
They look delicious.

00:13:12.950 --> 00:13:13.930
Thank you for the food.

00:13:19.900 --> 00:13:23.030
Sensei, is something wrong?

00:13:23.030 --> 00:13:24.410
What's wrong with this?

00:13:24.410 --> 00:13:25.950
It's spicy.

00:13:26.740 --> 00:13:29.450
<i>I tried putting wasabi in one of them.</i>

00:13:29.450 --> 00:13:31.800
<i>Why would you do that?</i>

00:13:31.800 --> 00:13:33.660
Who would do such a thing?!

00:13:33.660 --> 00:13:34.620
Hey...

00:13:35.660 --> 00:13:36.460
I'm here.

00:13:36.830 --> 00:13:39.170
Karen, welcome.

00:13:39.170 --> 00:13:40.930
I wish I could be a waitress.

00:13:40.930 --> 00:13:42.250
They look so cute.

00:13:42.670 --> 00:13:45.290
I think you'd be good with the customers, Karen.

00:13:46.050 --> 00:13:47.640
Welcome.

00:13:49.470 --> 00:13:51.640
What can I get you?

00:13:51.640 --> 00:13:53.890
Would you like dangos? Cake?

00:13:54.270 --> 00:13:55.570
Excuse me, sir!

00:13:55.570 --> 00:13:58.270
I'm not on the menu!

00:13:59.770 --> 00:14:00.810
How annoying.

00:14:08.700 --> 00:14:12.740
This is pretty different from our school.

00:14:12.740 --> 00:14:14.240
Oh, this is it.

00:14:15.200 --> 00:14:17.760
East-West, huh?

00:14:17.760 --> 00:14:19.750
Welcome, Master.

00:14:20.290 --> 00:14:21.670
That will be one tea, one coffee,

00:14:21.670 --> 00:14:24.660
a red bean cake, and chocolate dangos.

00:14:24.660 --> 00:14:27.260
It's pretty cute.

00:14:30.050 --> 00:14:31.680
There they are.

00:14:39.980 --> 00:14:45.130
I imagined Aya-chan would be wearing a Japanese outfit and Youko-chan would be a maid.

00:14:47.110 --> 00:14:49.280
You're acting way too suspicious.

00:14:49.280 --> 00:14:51.380
Aya-chan!

00:14:54.440 --> 00:14:56.420
Youko...

00:14:56.420 --> 00:14:59.540
I'll take care of this.

00:15:00.370 --> 00:15:03.400
Could you please refrain from taking pictures?

00:15:06.170 --> 00:15:07.340
Isa-nee!

00:15:07.340 --> 00:15:08.920
Ta-da.

00:15:08.920 --> 00:15:10.130
Isami.

00:15:10.770 --> 00:15:13.180
Onee-chan, you came?

00:15:13.180 --> 00:15:15.060
Isami.

00:15:17.060 --> 00:15:19.770
You look cute in traditional Japanese clothes, Alice.

00:15:20.480 --> 00:15:22.100
What about me?

00:15:22.100 --> 00:15:22.900
Huh?

00:15:22.900 --> 00:15:23.940
You look like you always do.

00:15:25.690 --> 00:15:27.500
No, you look cute.

00:15:30.110 --> 00:15:32.450
Shouldn't you two have dressed the other way around?

00:15:32.820 --> 00:15:35.870
T-That's what I originally intended...

00:15:35.870 --> 00:15:38.500
No, you look better in that.

00:15:38.500 --> 00:15:40.410
I'd like to try that outfit, too!

00:15:40.410 --> 00:15:42.910
Karen-chan, what is your class doing?

00:15:42.910 --> 00:15:43.920
A play.

00:15:43.920 --> 00:15:44.630
Oh, yeah!

00:15:44.630 --> 00:15:47.090
Isami, please come see me act.

00:15:47.920 --> 00:15:51.170
Take pictures of me with your camera.

00:15:51.550 --> 00:15:53.610
She's acting like an actress again.

00:15:58.560 --> 00:16:00.350
Our shifts are almost over.

00:16:00.350 --> 00:16:01.310
Already?

00:16:01.310 --> 00:16:04.270
Let's go check out the rest of the festival.

00:16:04.270 --> 00:16:05.980
Hey, it's a blonde girl!

00:16:05.980 --> 00:16:07.140
Thank you.

00:16:07.140 --> 00:16:08.360
The food was delicious.

00:16:12.770 --> 00:16:14.750
Thank you very much.

00:17:31.900 --> 00:17:33.650
What do you think, Alice?

00:17:33.650 --> 00:17:35.650
Are you enjoying the school festival?

00:17:35.650 --> 00:17:37.780
Yeah, it's delicious.

00:17:37.780 --> 00:17:39.200
I know, right?

00:17:39.780 --> 00:17:42.830
We've done nothing but eat for a while now.

00:17:44.140 --> 00:17:46.870
Karen's play is going to start soon.

00:17:47.500 --> 00:17:49.900
The play is Snow White.

00:17:50.890 --> 00:17:52.090
What a cliché.

00:17:52.090 --> 00:17:54.090
I wonder what role Karen is playing.

00:17:54.970 --> 00:17:58.430
I love Snow White.

00:17:59.550 --> 00:18:02.640
She loves all love stories.

00:18:10.940 --> 00:18:12.650
It's starting.

00:18:16.280 --> 00:18:17.820
Snow White...

00:18:17.820 --> 00:18:19.160
...is dead!

00:18:19.540 --> 00:18:21.160
Wait.

00:18:21.620 --> 00:18:25.300
I shall sever that witch's magic spell.

00:18:35.080 --> 00:18:38.550
Once again, I have cut a worthless object.

00:18:39.130 --> 00:18:41.550
<i>What is this?</i>

00:18:49.130 --> 00:18:51.440
Thank you.

00:18:54.270 --> 00:18:56.690
Kinda sad, isn't it?

00:18:56.690 --> 00:18:57.940
Yeah.

00:19:00.790 --> 00:19:02.500
<i>Oh, I forgot.</i>

00:19:04.080 --> 00:19:06.450
<i>I need to give her that gift.</i>

00:19:12.040 --> 00:19:18.510
Shi...

00:19:21.550 --> 00:19:26.430
I keep feeling like I can hear whispers of "death, death..."

00:19:26.430 --> 00:19:27.970
What? That's terrifying!

00:19:33.360 --> 00:19:36.480
I didn't move fast enough, and now the school festival's over.

00:19:36.940 --> 00:19:38.780
Alice.

00:19:38.780 --> 00:19:41.490
Let's go throw out the trash together.

00:19:44.310 --> 00:19:45.800
<i>This is my chance.</i>

00:19:45.800 --> 00:19:46.910
Hm?

00:19:46.910 --> 00:19:49.870
Alice, what do you have in your hand?

00:19:50.210 --> 00:19:51.960
Is it garbage?

00:19:51.960 --> 00:19:53.630
Let's throw it away with the rest of the garbage.

00:19:56.000 --> 00:19:58.930
Did I say the wrong thing again?

00:19:58.930 --> 00:19:59.770
Shino.

00:19:59.770 --> 00:20:00.870
Y-Yes?

00:20:02.980 --> 00:20:07.760
P-Please... Please accept this gift.

00:20:08.850 --> 00:20:10.120
A present?

00:20:10.720 --> 00:20:11.640
For me?

00:20:11.640 --> 00:20:13.890
Y-Yeah.

00:20:13.890 --> 00:20:18.650
You gave me this hairpin before, remember?

00:20:18.650 --> 00:20:22.010
I've always wanted to thank you for it.

00:20:24.240 --> 00:20:27.120
I hope you like it.

00:20:36.040 --> 00:20:37.250
An angel...

00:20:37.630 --> 00:20:40.170
A little blonde angel...

00:20:40.170 --> 00:20:42.630
Shino, pull yourself together!

00:20:45.800 --> 00:20:47.180
What a cute ribbon.

00:20:48.430 --> 00:20:51.890
You wear the hairpin I gave you every day,

00:20:51.890 --> 00:20:54.800
so I'll wear this ribbon and make it my charm point.

00:20:55.520 --> 00:20:56.730
How does it look?

00:20:56.730 --> 00:20:58.450
It's cute.

00:20:58.450 --> 00:21:00.390
It looks great.

00:21:01.900 --> 00:21:05.280
Thanks for waiting.

00:21:05.280 --> 00:21:06.740
You're late.

00:21:12.340 --> 00:21:13.410
Shino.

00:21:13.410 --> 00:21:14.940
What's with your hair?

00:21:14.940 --> 00:21:15.920
Are you fishing for laughs?

00:21:18.000 --> 00:21:19.920
A top knot!

00:21:21.860 --> 00:21:25.050
Is this a display ribbon?

00:21:25.050 --> 00:21:26.350
Why?

00:21:26.350 --> 00:21:28.930
But it's so cute!

00:22:59.310 --> 00:23:02.170
There's a Japanese expression that I really like recently.

00:23:02.170 --> 00:23:03.020
What is it?

00:23:03.020 --> 00:23:04.900
"Donmai".

00:23:05.360 --> 00:23:09.360
It's a magic phrase that cheers you up even when you're feeling down.

00:23:09.360 --> 00:23:10.280
Really?

00:23:16.540 --> 00:23:19.910
Japanese is amazing.

00:23:20.550 --> 00:23:22.560
Shino, do you have any anniversaries?

00:23:22.560 --> 00:23:25.370
Since you arrived, every day has been an anniversary!

00:23:25.370 --> 00:23:26.060
Shino...

00:23:26.060 --> 00:23:27.380
But if I had to choose something...

00:23:27.380 --> 00:23:30.500
The new brand of instant noodles I had last week was delicious,

00:23:30.500 --> 00:23:31.910
so I might make that my ramen...

00:23:31.910 --> 00:23:33.110
...noodleversary!

00:23:33.110 --> 00:23:34.440
Good night.
